-- When the operator restricted the account at the person's request (GDPR Art. 18, `erase restrict`): while it is set the pool keeps the account's data stored and takes nothing more. A deposit, a raw part, and a telemetry batch naming the account are refused 403 `account_restricted`, and its records no longer count toward a shared cell. Its export, an erasure, the withdrawal sweep, and the retention sweeps still run. Milliseconds; null when the account is not restricted. No credential is revoked, so lifting it (set to null) restores the account whole.
ALTER TABLE accounts ADD COLUMN restricted_at INTEGER;
